  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Clue is an artifact type. Even though it appears on some cards with other permanent types, it's never a creature type, a land type, or anything but an artifact type.",
      "oracle_id": "2d16d51b-47e0-4cdc-83dd-a805ba50bd83",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect refers to a Clue, it means any Clue artifact, not just a Clue artifact token. For example, you can sacrifice Wrench to pay for Alquist Proft, Master Sleuth's activated ability.",
      "oracle_id": "2d16d51b-47e0-4cdc-83dd-a805ba50bd83",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you target a creature with ward, you may still pay the ward cost, but Out Cold won't be countered even if you don't.",
      "oracle_id": "2d16d51b-47e0-4cdc-83dd-a805ba50bd83",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Some abilities trigger \"whenever you sacrifice a Clue\". Those abilities trigger whenever you sacrifice a Clue for any reason, not just to activate a Clue's activated ability.",
      "oracle_id": "2d16d51b-47e0-4cdc-83dd-a805ba50bd83",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Some spells and abilities that investigate may require targets. If each target chosen is an illegal target as that spell or ability tries to resolve, it won't resolve. You won't create any Clue tokens.",
      "oracle_id": "2d16d51b-47e0-4cdc-83dd-a805ba50bd83",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't sacrifice a Clue to pay multiple costs. For example, you can't sacrifice a Clue token to activate its own ability and also to activate Alquist Proft, Master Sleuth's ability.",
      "oracle_id": "2d16d51b-47e0-4cdc-83dd-a805ba50bd83",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You don't have to choose any targets for Out Cold. However, if you do, and all of those creatures are illegal targets at the time Out Cold tries to resolve, it won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won't investigate.",
      "oracle_id": "2d16d51b-47e0-4cdc-83dd-a805ba50bd83",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Abilities that trigger when a permanent \"becomes untapped\" won't trigger if a stun counter is removed instead.",
      "oracle_id": "4640ce0e-f82f-4bfd-93fc-2d865863fc2e",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a permanent has more than one stun counter on it, only one will be removed each time it would become untapped.",
      "oracle_id": "4640ce0e-f82f-4bfd-93fc-2d865863fc2e",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a tapped permanent with a stun counter on it would become untapped, a stun counter will be removed from it instead. This is a replacement effect.",
      "oracle_id": "4640ce0e-f82f-4bfd-93fc-2d865863fc2e",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If untapping a permanent is part of a cost (such as that of Halo Fountain's first ability), you may pay that cost by \"untapping\" a tapped permanent with a stun counter on it. The stun counter will be removed and the creature will remain tapped. However, the cost will still be paid.",
      "oracle_id": "4640ce0e-f82f-4bfd-93fc-2d865863fc2e",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "On the other hand, if untapping multiple permanents is part of a cost (such as that of Halo Fountain's last two abilities), you can't \"untap\" the same permanent more than once to pay that cost.",
      "oracle_id": "4640ce0e-f82f-4bfd-93fc-2d865863fc2e",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Stun counters are not keyword counters, and they don't cause the permanents they're on to gain any abilities. They won't be affected by effects that cause permanents to lose all abilities.",
      "oracle_id": "4640ce0e-f82f-4bfd-93fc-2d865863fc2e",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Stun counters exist independently of the effects that created them. If a permanent has no stun counters on it, it will untap as normal.",
      "oracle_id": "4640ce0e-f82f-4bfd-93fc-2d865863fc2e",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Stun counters replace untapping for any reason, including players untapping tapped permanents during their untap steps.",
      "oracle_id": "4640ce0e-f82f-4bfd-93fc-2d865863fc2e",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Must target two different creatures.",
      "oracle_id": "506ea048-aca5-439a-a5b5-059ddda0672a",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You may target creatures that are already tapped with Succumb to the Cold. If a target creature is already tapped as it resolves, you will still put a stun counter on it.",
      "oracle_id": "73992788-8084-459c-8375-9ccc8579c5d7",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the copy says that it affects \"you,\" it affects the controller of the copy, not the controller of the original spell. Similarly, if the copy says that it affects an \"opponent,\" it affects an opponent of the copy's controller, not an opponent of the original spell's controller.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca",
      "published_at": "2010-08-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the spell Reverberate copies has an X whose value was determined as it was cast (like Earthquake does), the copy has the same value of X.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca",
      "published_at": "2010-08-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the spell Reverberate copies is modal (that is, it says \"Choose one \u2014\" or the like), the copy will have the same mode. You can't choose a different one.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca",
      "published_at": "2010-08-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Reverberate can target (and copy) any instant or sorcery spell, not just one with targets. It doesn't matter who controls it.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca",
      "published_at": "2010-08-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The copy will have the same targets as the spell it's copying unless you choose new ones. You may change any number of the targets, including all of them or none of them. If, for one of the targets, you can't choose a new legal target, then it remains unchanged (even if the current target is illegal).",
      "oracle_id": "a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca",
      "published_at": "2010-08-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When Reverberate resolves, it creates a copy of a spell. You control the copy. That copy is created on the stack, so it's not \"cast.\" Abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell won't trigger. The copy will then resolve like a normal spell, after players get a chance to cast spells and activate abilities.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca",
      "published_at": "2010-08-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't choose to pay any additional costs for the copy. However, effects based on any additional costs that were paid for the original spell are copied as though those same costs were paid for the copy too. For example, if a player sacrifices a 3/3 creature to cast Fling, and you copy it with Reverberate, the copy of Fling will also deal 3 damage to its target.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca",
      "published_at": "2010-08-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If all of the target creatures are illegal targets as Rime Chill tries to resolve, it won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won't draw a card.",
      "oracle_id": "bad84deb-3f2c-46fd-9dcb-4e3ba9732769",
      "published_at": "2025-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Lands are normally colorless permanents, even if they tap for mana of a certain color.",
      "oracle_id": "bad84deb-3f2c-46fd-9dcb-4e3ba9732769",
      "published_at": "2025-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The colors are white, blue, black, red, and green. Colorless is not a color.",
      "oracle_id": "bad84deb-3f2c-46fd-9dcb-4e3ba9732769",
      "published_at": "2025-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "382097b3-f753-493c-bde4-101c0538feb4",
      "published_at": "2020-06-23",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Frost Breath can target tapped creatures. If a targeted creature is already tapped when the spell resolves, that creature just remains tapped and doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "32e915fb-3836-4bed-93b1-61c9c3951ad1",
      "published_at": "2013-09-15",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "You choose how to order cards returned to your library after scrying no matter where you put them."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "32e915fb-3836-4bed-93b1-61c9c3951ad1",
      "published_at": "2013-09-15",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Scry appears on some spells and abilities with one or more targets. If all of the spell or ability’s targets are illegal when it tries to resolve, it won’t resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won’t scry."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "32e915fb-3836-4bed-93b1-61c9c3951ad1",
      "published_at": "2013-09-15",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "You perform the actions stated on a card in sequence. For some spells and abilities, that means you’ll scry last. For others, that means you’ll scry and then perform other actions."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "32e915fb-3836-4bed-93b1-61c9c3951ad1",
      "published_at": "2013-09-15",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "When you scry, you may put all the cards you look at back on top of your library, you may put all of those cards on the bottom of your library, or you may put some of those cards on top and the rest of them on the bottom."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "32e915fb-3836-4bed-93b1-61c9c3951ad1",
      "published_at": "2014-02-01",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If a creature affected by Sudden Storm changes controllers before its old controller’s next untap step, Sudden Storm will prevent it from becoming untapped during its new controller’s next untap step."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "32e915fb-3836-4bed-93b1-61c9c3951ad1",
      "published_at": "2014-02-01",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If you chose two targets and one is an illegal target when Sudden Storm resolves, that creature won’t become tapped and it won’t be stopped from untapping during its controller’s next untap step. It won’t be affected by Sudden Storm in any way."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "32e915fb-3836-4bed-93b1-61c9c3951ad1",
      "published_at": "2014-02-01",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "This spell can target tapped creatures. If a targeted creature is already tapped when the spell resolves, that creature remains tapped and doesn’t untap during its controller’s next untap step."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "32e915fb-3836-4bed-93b1-61c9c3951ad1",
      "published_at": "2014-02-01",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If you choose zero targets, you’ll just scry 1 when the ability resolves. However, if you choose at least one target and all of Sudden Storm’s targets are illegal as it tries to resolve, the spell won’t resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won’t scry in that case."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "057729d0-f7ed-465b-91aa-fb2c6d6612b2",
      "published_at": "2021-04-16",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If you chose targets for Snow Day as you cast it, and none of those targets are legal as it tries to resolve, it will be removed from the stack and do nothing. You will not draw or discard."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "057729d0-f7ed-465b-91aa-fb2c6d6612b2",
      "published_at": "2021-04-16",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "You may choose tapped creatures as targets. Those creatures won’t untap during their controller’s next untap step."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "d5cdfa86-a234-4ddd-bfa0-4a3bc51eebce",
      "published_at": "2022-02-18",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If a channel ability requires a target, you may not activate it without a target just to discard the card."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "d5cdfa86-a234-4ddd-bfa0-4a3bc51eebce",
      "published_at": "2022-02-18",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Discarding the card is part of the cost to activate a channel ability."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "7a5a81f7-1597-4972-8565-fd2a5667df99",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Sacrificing an Eldrazi Scion creature token to add {C} is a mana ability. It doesn't use the stack and can't be responded to."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "7a5a81f7-1597-4972-8565-fd2a5667df99",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "A card with devoid is just colorless. It's not colorless and the colors of mana in its mana cost."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "7a5a81f7-1597-4972-8565-fd2a5667df99",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Adverse Conditions tracks the creatures, but not their controller. If either of the creatures changes controllers before its first controller's next untap step has come around, then it won't untap during its new controller's next untap step."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "7a5a81f7-1597-4972-8565-fd2a5667df99",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "You can cast Adverse Conditions with no targets. When it resolves, you'll get an Eldrazi Scion. However, if you cast Adverse Conditions with any targets and all of those targets are illegal as it tries to resolve, it won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won't get the Eldrazi Scion in that case."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "7a5a81f7-1597-4972-8565-fd2a5667df99",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Eldrazi Scions are similar to Eldrazi Spawn, seen in the Zendikar block. Note that Eldrazi Scions are 1/1, not 0/1."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "7a5a81f7-1597-4972-8565-fd2a5667df99",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Eldrazi and Scion are each separate creature types. Anything that affects Eldrazi will affect these tokens, for example."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "7a5a81f7-1597-4972-8565-fd2a5667df99",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Some instants and sorceries that create Eldrazi Scions require targets. If all targets for such a spell have become illegal by the time that spell tries to resolve, the spell won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won't get any Eldrazi Scions."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "7a5a81f7-1597-4972-8565-fd2a5667df99",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Devoid works in all zones, not just on the battlefield."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "7a5a81f7-1597-4972-8565-fd2a5667df99",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If a card loses devoid, it will still be colorless. This is because effects that change an object's color (like the one created by devoid) are considered before the object loses devoid."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "7a5a81f7-1597-4972-8565-fd2a5667df99",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Other cards and abilities can give a card with devoid color. If that happens, it's just the new color, not that color and colorless."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "7a5a81f7-1597-4972-8565-fd2a5667df99",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Cards with devoid use frames that are variations of the transparent frame traditionally used for Eldrazi. The top part of the card features some color over a background based on the texture of the hedrons that once imprisoned the Eldrazi. This coloration is intended to aid deckbuilding and game play."
    }
  ],
